# =====================================================================
# ELKH Project Encoding Standards (Added for encoding consistency)
# =====================================================================
# This section enforces UTF-8 encoding for all text files to prevent
# encoding issues discovered in 2026 encoding audit.
# 
# Key benefits:
# - Prevents smart quotes and Unicode character issues
# - Ensures consistent team collaboration across different systems
# - Maintains proper handling of international content
#
# IMPORTANT: Team members should configure their editors to:
# 1. Use UTF-8 encoding by default
# 2. Show invisible characters to detect encoding issues
# 3. Replace smart quotes with ASCII quotes automatically
# 4. Replace Unicode box drawing characters with ASCII equivalents
#
# Reference: See encoding-issues-report.md for complete analysis
# Automated fix available: run fix-encoding-issues.ps1 for bulk corrections
# =====================================================================

# Ensure all PowerShell scripts use UTF-8 with BOM for better Windows compatibility
*.ps1 text eol=crlf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Special handling for appsettings files (critical for ELKH project)
appsettings*.json text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Ensure seeding files maintain UTF-8 encoding
*Seeder*.cs text diff=csharp working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
